Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 07:54:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] www: header pills - English never cut, Firmware shows the
 Reaper version (102.8 line)

Owner report: header words were cut in English. Measured on a 1920x1080
canvas (and 1536 / 1366) in EN, RU, DE and FR through the language mock.

- The Firmware pill shows the Reaper version alone (Reaper_v3.6.0); the
  BETA tag keeps the pre-release mark and the whole string is on hover.
- Each pill label, and the two translated values (WAN state, operating
  mode), carry their English text in data-en. fit.js never cuts one below
  that English width (capped at the text itself, so a short word is never
  padded): English is the standard size, a longer translation gives way
  down to it.
- The pill strip (data-rfit-strip) drops pills from the end by what the
  English sizes need, replacing the fixed 1700/1450/1280 breakpoints, so
  English is never cut at any width and every language shows the same
  pills.

Result: 1920 - every language in full; 1536 and 1366 - English in full,
RU/FR trimmed only where the word is longer than the English.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
